## 1. Token principles

- **Three tiers, always.** Primitive → Semantic/alias → Component. Consumers and screens
  bind to **semantic** tokens; raw primitives are never applied directly in a screen or a
  component where a semantic exists.
- **Alias chain:** Semantic → Tokens → Primitives. A semantic token's value is an alias,
  not a literal, unless it is itself a primitive.
- **Naming taxonomy:** `Category/Concept-Property` — e.g. `Surface/Brand-Primary`,
  `Text/Error/Default`, `Border-Radius/*`, `Border-Width/*`, `Scale/*`. New tokens match
  the existing pattern; no ad-hoc names. ({{TOKEN_PREFIXES}})
- **Intent families are complete and symmetric.** Every intent — success, warning, error,
  info, disabled — carries the full set: `Surface/* · Text/* · Border/* · Icon/*`.
- **Scales, not magic numbers.** Spacing on a 4/8 base via `Scale/*`. Type on a modular
  scale (text styles, not inline sizes). Radius and border-width tokenized. Any literal in
  a component is a finding.
- **Brand decisions enter only as tokens.** A color or type choice from `brand-designer` is
  encoded as a semantic token here before any component uses it.

