## 2. Component & pattern conventions

- **Atomic Design placement.** Classify each as atom / molecule / organism; compose from
  smaller pieces, never duplicate.
- **Orthogonal variant axes.** Axes are independent and single-responsibility. EXTEND an
  existing component's axis before spawning a new component. Watch for combinatorial blow-up.
- **Anatomy & API.** Named slots; boolean toggles for optional parts; instance-swap where
  it fits. Component-property names are consistent across the system.
- **State completeness.** Interactive components carry default / hover / focus / active /
  disabled / error where relevant.
- **Canonical components are mandatory in screens.** Inner header → the canonical inner-header
  variant. Menu row → the canonical list-item variant. Hero amount → the canonical amount
  input. Confirmation → the canonical dialog + illustration swap. Hand-built equivalents are
  drift.

