## 6. Evaluation frameworks (the heuristic canon)

Beyond the system benchmarks (§3), {{SYSTEM_NAME}} evaluates design against five established heuristic
frameworks. **DESIGN.md still wins on conflict (§3.1)** — these inform the agents' lenses, they
don't override {{SYSTEM_NAME}} rulings. Apply each **at the layer it governs**: the system / component /
brand parts run in this context; several principles are screen- and flow-level and therefore
belong to the **separate screen-creation context**, not this one.

- **Dieter Rams — 10 Principles for Good Design** — the *ethos* for the whole system: useful,
  understandable, unobtrusive, honest, thorough to the last detail, long-lasting, and **as little
  design as possible**. North star for `ds-steward` (restraint — no decorative tokens/variants;
  generalize, don't special-case) and `brand-designer` (aesthetic + honest expression).
- **Shneiderman — 8 Golden Rules.** *Component layer* (`ds-steward` bakes in): **consistency**
  (uniform anatomy/naming/behavior), **informative feedback** (state set per §2.4), **simple error
  handling + easy reversal** (error states, undo affordances), **reduce short-term memory load**
  (self-describing component APIs). *Screen layer* (separate context): dialogue **closure**,
  **shortcuts** for frequent users, **internal locus of control** across a flow.
- **Tognazzini — First Principles.** **Color** (functional, accessible, secondary to content) is a
  `ds-steward` + `brand-designer` rule (§1, §4). *Anticipation, autonomy, efficiency of the user,
  visible navigation (You-Are-Here), explorable interfaces* are screen-level → separate context.
- **Gerhardt-Powals — Cognitive Engineering.** Reduce cognitive load: **automate unwanted workload,
  reduce uncertainty, fuse data, present new information with meaningful aids.** `ds-steward`
  applies these to *pattern* design (clear states, sensible defaults, data-display components);
  screen composition applies them in the separate context.
- **Weinschenk & Barker — Classification.** **Accessibility · Error Prevention · User Feedback** are
  carried at the *source* by `ds-steward` (§4 + component states), so screens inherit them.
  **Navigation · System Capabilities** are screen/flow-level → separate context.

**Layer map — use it where it's needed:**

| Layer | Heuristics applied here | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| Token / system ethos | Rams (restraint, honesty, thoroughness); Tognazzini Color | `ds-steward` |
| Component interaction | Shneiderman (consistency, feedback, error/reversal, memory load); Gerhardt-Powals (reduce uncertainty, meaningful aids); Weinschenk (accessibility, error prevention, feedback) | `ds-steward` |
| Brand / expression | Rams (innovative, aesthetic, unobtrusive, honest, long-lasting); Tognazzini Color | `brand-designer` |
| Screen / flow | Shneiderman (closure, shortcuts, locus of control); Tognazzini (anticipation, autonomy, navigation, explorability, efficiency); Gerhardt-Powals (fuse data, automate workload); Weinschenk (navigation, system capabilities) | **separate screen-creation context** |

**Operationalized per pipeline step** in `AGENTS-HANDOFF.md` → *Heuristic canon per pipeline step*:
which slice fires at the brand decision · tokenize/build/bind · binding-gate/publish · drift-check/commit.

