## How agents use this file

- `ds-steward` — reads §1–§6 at plan and as the pre-publish gate (the `system_design_lens`),
  applying the system + component layer of §6.
- `component-designer` — reads §1–§4 + §6 (the component-layer slice): how to build + bind to meet
  the token standards, state completeness, and accessibility baseline.
- `brand-designer` — reads §1 + §6 (Rams + Tognazzini Color): how a brand decision becomes a token,
  and proposes additions here when setting new expressive direction.

DESIGN.md is shared ground truth. The **separate screen-creation context** (screen building +
flows/specs) also reads it — §2 (canonical components), §4 (accessibility / interaction
conventions), and the **screen-level** heuristics of §6 — but those roles live outside this
design-system context.
